                <pb facs="0616" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/827: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-31T18:00:00+09:00">December 31, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 31—7:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>818. Department’s 435, December 30, 7 p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d808-f1"/> The
                    organic regulations of the China Board were promulgated on December 16 on which
                    date the Board was organized and began to function. Our despatch 3549, December
                        23<anchor n="25" xml:id="d808-f2"/> on this subject was sent forward in the
                    pouch leaving on the day following.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
